# --- Editor state -----------------------------------------------------------
# Obsidian keeps per-machine UI state here. It churns on every open and is
# never worth a commit; the rest of .obsidian/ is your config and IS worth it.
# Rules for other editors belong alongside these — this file is not
# Obsidian-specific, Obsidian is just the case that needs rules.
.obsidian/workspace.json
.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json
.obsidian/cache
.trash/

# --- Credentials ------------------------------------------------------------
# Some editor plugins store API tokens in plaintext. If one ever does, ignore
# that plugin's folder specifically rather than committing the token into a
# repo that may later be pushed.
# .obsidian/plugins/<plugin-name>/data.json

